# The function, its prototype object and its objects stay with compiled code, and `weigh` holds one function: compiled code takes `weigh` for that function, finds nothing under `late`, and takes the `prototype` property to be as it was made, all without a look.
# `kind` holds no function, so the record of the class does not declare it. The image lists it beside the record, and every other name stays ruled out.
# `poke` is a free name that each run defines, and it is handed nothing. It climbs from an object that it takes out of the heap: another function under `weigh`, a name that the program does not lay, another object in the `prototype` property are ruled out and end the process.
# The same function stored again, a store under `kind` and another `constructor` go through.
# The green twin: deeds-on-a-constructor-function-that-unseen-code-was-handed-go-through.ir.
